    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "FOR A/C\n8763\n8765\n8766\nONLY\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nCAPITOL\nINTERNATIONAL AIRWAYS\nForm No. G-420\n(Oct. 1, 1978)\nA\nEXIT\nEXIT\nWINDOW EXIT\nC\nEXIT\nDOOR EXIT\nSEAT BELTS\nFASTEN\nPull handle up\nand over. Push\ndoor out.\nKeep seat belt fastened\nwhen seated\nUNFASTEN\nDOOR EXITS AND ESCAPE SLIDES\n2.\nPull Red Handle to\ninflate slide.\n3.\nRemove shoes and\nall sharp objects.\nBRACE POSITION\n4. Jump and sit in slide.\nB.\nPull window handle in\nand down.\nNO SHOES\nESCAPE WINDOWS OVER WINGS\nRemove shoes\nand all sharp\nobjects.\n3.\nDiscard window through\nopening, and exit through\nwindow.\nAt rear of wing.\nslide down flaps.\nNO SHOES\nAUXILIARY DOOR EXITS AND ESCAPE SLIDES\n1. Pull handle in\nand down.\n2.\nLet go of handle when\nexit starts to fall out.\n3.\nRemove shoes and\nall sharp objects.\nJump and sit\nin slide.\nNO SHOES\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT",
      "NO RADIOS\nFOR A/C 8763, 8765, 8766 ONLY\nNO ELECTRIC\nNO VISIBLE\nCOMPUTERS\nFLUID LIGHTERS\n244677\nPLEASE DO NOT\nREMOVE THIS CARD\nFROM AIRCRAFT\nOxygen masks are located\nin a compartment above each\nrow of passenger seats.\nNo smoking while\noxygen is in use.\nOXYGEN\n3. When oxygen masks\nappear, properly place\nthe mask over nose and\nmouth and breathe\nnormally.\n4. How to adjust mask.\nOnce mask is in place, it\nmay be adjusted by\npulling on the elastic\nhead band.\nIndividual life vest\nis under each seat.\nPULL TAB FOR VEST\n2.\nLIFE VEST\nPut on life vest over\nyour head. Pull waist straps\nfrom back and fasten hooks\ninto rings\n3.\nPull straps until they\nare very snug aroung\nwaist.\nLIGHT\nTo inflate life vest\npull downward on\nthe two red knobs\nat the bottom of\nvest.\nLIFE RAFT CEILING COMPARTMENT\nTo open ceiling raft\ncompartment, pull this\nhandle down.\n2.\nLift raft off compartment\ndoor and launch out nearest\nexit.\nHOW TO INFLATE RAFT\nWhen raft is launched into water it\nis secured to the airplane by a tape\nTo avoid inflating the raft inside the\nairplane do not lift or drag raft by this\nTape.\nTo inflate raft, lift this flap and pull\nring and cable all the way out.\n25\nMan Raft\nADDITIONAL LIFE RAFTS\nLOCATED IN AFT CLOSET\nNO SHOES\nRADIO BEACON TRANSMITTER\nCOIL SPRING\nANTENNA\nRADIO BEACON TRANSMITTER\nLOCATED IN COCKPIT BULKHEAD\nLANYARD\nHOLES FOR WATER ENTRANCE\nTO ACTIVATE BATTERY\nСАРІтОк\nINTERNATIONAL AIRWAYS\n2002.127.191"
    ],
